# Portfolio 2026

## Do not assume — ask

When a choice changes look, architecture, published content, or interaction, ask before implementing. Do not silently invent typography, copy, name/links, crop policy, or effect parameters as "final."

## Never ship AI artifacts

- Do not commit or deploy `portfolio_cursor_plan.md`, chat dumps, agent notes, or hidden plan files.
- Keep working notes under gitignored `notes/` only.

## Assets stay out of git

- Never commit `sample_imgs/`, `assets/originals/`, or `assets/prepared/` atlases.
- Prepared media for production goes to CDN/Blob/R2; the Vercel app is `site/` only.

## Phase gates

- Prefer a runnable visual slice over infrastructure sprawl.
- Stationary grid language: cells stay fixed; content changes in place (not tile strafing).
- Organization (what goes where), transition (how cells morph), and atmosphere (haze/halo) stay separately tunable.
- Identity/UI is readable HTML/CSS independent of shaders.
- No sound in v1. No CMS, auth, or cloud ML embeddings unless explicitly requested.
